    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n19479" root="سربل" body-key="s">
    
      Q. 2 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَسَرْبَلَ</span></b> , (S,) or <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَسَرْبَلَ سِرْبَالًا</span> (Msb) or
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بِسِرْبَالٍ</span>, (M, K,) <i>He clad himself,</i> or <i>became clad,
with a</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سِرْبَال</span>: (S, M, Msb, K:) and so <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَسَرْبَنَ</span>, in
which, accord. to Yaakoob, the <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ن</span> is a substitute
for the <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ل</span> of the former. (M.)

